WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.480
Your goal should not be to look

00:00:02.159 --> 00:00:06.319
successful. It should be to build true

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:08.480
wealth. And I learned that lesson

00:00:06.319 --> 00:00:10.160
through a lot of my own mistakes. So

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:12.880
today, I'm going to be breaking down

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:15.280
four reasons why looking poor and

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:17.039
keeping a low profile can actually be

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:19.279
one of the smartest wealth building

00:00:17.039 --> 00:00:21.680
strategies that there is and how it

00:00:19.279 --> 00:00:23.840
keeps you out of the endless cycle of

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.840
upgrading your life instead of growing

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:28.480
your money. Reason number one, there is

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:30.160
a stress tax on fake wealth. You've

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:32.320
probably seen this play out in your own

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:34.640
life. We hit a milestone. We get a

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:36.559
raise, a promotion, a bigger paycheck,

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:38.160
and then our standards almost change

00:00:36.559 --> 00:00:40.320
immediately. And for a really short

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.719
period of time, it feels great, but then

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:44.800
it fades. The excitement wears off. The

00:00:42.719 --> 00:00:46.640
dopamine kind of settles, and now you're

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:48.719
comparing yourself to a new group of

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:51.120
people. And this is what is known as the

00:00:48.719 --> 00:00:53.039
hyonic treadmill. And the concept really

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:55.840
is that you adapt quickly to new

00:00:53.039 --> 00:00:57.760
purchases and the thrill disappears

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:59.760
faster than you expected it to. No

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:02.160
matter how much you spend or how many

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:04.640
highs you chase, you eventually return

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:06.880
to the same baseline level of happiness

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:08.960
regardless of the stuff that you own.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:10.720
From a money perspective, this is really

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:13.040
dangerous because every time we raise

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:15.760
our lifestyle baseline, we lock in

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:17.840
higher expenses, but we don't lock in

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:20.080
higher satisfaction. That's why people

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:22.479
can double their income and still feel

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:24.960
just as stressed out, maybe even more

00:01:22.479 --> 00:01:27.280
stressed out. In fact, around 78% of

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:29.040
people report feeling stressed trying to

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:31.040
keep up with the lifestyle of their

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:33.680
social circle. What used to feel like

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:35.680
success becomes your new normal. Let's

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:37.680
go even deeper about the hidden cost of

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:40.079
all that stuff because not everything

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:42.159
you buy adds value to your life. A lot

00:01:40.079 --> 00:01:44.079
of it just adds noise. Every physical

00:01:42.159 --> 00:01:45.759
item that you own comes with a mental

00:01:44.079 --> 00:01:47.280
contract that you didn't really realize

00:01:45.759 --> 00:01:49.439
that you signed. You're agreeing to

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:51.280
clean it, to fix it, to ensure it, to

00:01:49.439 --> 00:01:53.439
store it, and ultimately to think about

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:55.439
it. You buy the bigger house, now you've

00:01:53.439 --> 00:01:57.600
got a bigger roof that can leak and you

00:01:55.439 --> 00:01:59.520
got more AC units to break and a lawn

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:01.680
that constantly needs mowing. On

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:03.759
average, homeowners spend about 300

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:05.439
hours every year just maintaining their

00:02:03.759 --> 00:02:07.360
home. And if you do the math on that,

00:02:05.439 --> 00:02:10.160
that's 12 1/2 days out of the year,

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:12.640
which is like 3 and 12% of your entire

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:15.040
year. Think about that. We confuse net

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:16.959
worth with our self-worth. And if you're

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:19.280
not careful, what you really end up with

00:02:16.959 --> 00:02:21.120
is net stress. If something doesn't

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:22.879
meaningfully improve your happiness,

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:25.040
your health, or your freedom, it really

00:02:22.879 --> 00:02:27.200
is not an asset. It is a drain on your

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:29.280
energy. Reason number two is that you

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:31.599
lose your freedom of choice. When you

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:34.000
keep chasing a lifestyle, your freedom

00:02:31.599 --> 00:02:37.599
disappears slowly, but it compounds so

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:39.760
fast. Roughly 60 to 65% of US workers

00:02:37.599 --> 00:02:42.080
say they feel trapped or shackled to

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:44.239
their jobs, largely because of financial

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:46.720
pressure. And this is not just a US

00:02:44.239 --> 00:02:49.280
problem. Globally, nearly two billion

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:51.360
people work in informal or unstable

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:53.760
employment. Often not because they want

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:56.160
to, but because it's a last resort

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:57.680
option for survival, not a free choice.

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:59.840
And here's what that looks like in real

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:02.080
life. You can't take breaks. You can't

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:03.840
pivot. You can't really walk away from

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:05.519
work that you hate because you

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:08.000
ultimately need the paycheck. And I've

00:03:05.519 --> 00:03:10.319
fallen into this trap myself many times.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:12.720
I was working non-stop and making good

00:03:10.319 --> 00:03:14.720
money, but I wasn't keeping nearly as

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:16.560
much as I should have. And over time, I

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:19.280
realized I couldn't step away. I had to

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:21.840
be there early, stay late, and say yes,

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:24.560
even when I wanted to say no. I wasn't a

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:26.800
CEO. I was an employee of my own

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:28.879
overhead and my own expenses. And

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:31.040
there's a serious cost to that when you

00:03:28.879 --> 00:03:33.120
zoom out. On average, people spend about

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:35.040
90,000 hours working over their

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:37.040
lifetime, which is roughly onethird of

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:38.959
their adult life. And the main takeaway

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:41.519
from all this is that once you stop

00:03:38.959 --> 00:03:43.840
spending on things like expensive car

00:03:41.519 --> 00:03:46.480
loans, designer clothes, and fancy

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:49.280
trips, your required income actually

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:51.920
drops drastically. When you need less,

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:53.920
work has less control over you. And that

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:56.080
is how you can earn freedom. It's also

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:58.000
why some folks retire in their 50s while

00:03:56.080 --> 00:04:00.239
others work into their 60s and their

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:02.080
70s. Reason number three, it creates

00:04:00.239 --> 00:04:04.080
liquidity for opportunities. And this

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:05.760
one's a big one. So, most millionaires

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:07.760
didn't get wealthy from their earned

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:11.120
income. They built their wealth through

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:13.040
assets. And assets require timing and

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:14.640
capital. Opportunities don't really show

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:16.400
up when it's convenient, right? Like, we

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:18.320
can all agree on that. They show up

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:19.759
during uncertainty. We've all heard the

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:21.919
saying of Warren Buffett, right?

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:24.000
Opportunities come infrequently. When it

00:04:21.919 --> 00:04:25.520
rains gold, put out the bucket. The

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:27.199
problem is is that most people don't

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:29.199
have a bucket. They have a lot of

00:04:27.199 --> 00:04:31.120
expenses and a lot of overhead. When the

00:04:29.199 --> 00:04:33.520
market crashes or real estate takes a

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:35.440
dip, the guy with the least Lambo is

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:37.040
panicking. He's in fight or flight,

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:39.360
right? But the guy driving the

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:41.360
10-year-old truck, he's not panicking.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:43.680
He's buying the Lambo driver's rental

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:46.000
property at a 30% discount. One example

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:48.400
is looking back at the pandemic, the S&P

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:50.639
500 dropped like 30%. If you would have

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:52.880
bought that dip knowing Warren Buffett's

00:04:50.639 --> 00:04:55.040
other saying, be fearful when people are

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:57.120
greedy and be greedy when people are

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:58.960
fearful, then when there's all this fear

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:00.400
in the market, if you had 10 grand

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:02.160
sitting on the sidelines because you

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:04.320
were liquid, you weren't blowing all of

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:06.240
your money, you could buy in and in a

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:09.440
matter of 6 months, I guarantee you you

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:11.280
make 50, 60, 70% on your money in

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:13.440
situations like that. That is what

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:16.479
liquidity does. It turns economic

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:18.160
crisises or even bad headlines into

00:05:16.479 --> 00:05:20.160
clearance sales. But if all your money

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:22.080
is tied up in a lifestyle, then you're

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:24.000
forced to sit on the sidelines when the

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:26.000
opportunity of a lifetime actually walks

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:27.919
right in front of you. Because cash is

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:30.160
ultimately leverage. Some of the best

00:05:27.919 --> 00:05:32.720
opportunities are really simple. People

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:34.960
needing quick cash sell assets below

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:36.320
market value every single day. I own a

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:38.479
big real estate company where we

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:40.400
literally specialize in buying assets

00:05:38.479 --> 00:05:42.720
below market value. If all your money is

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:45.280
tied up in lifestyle, car payments,

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:47.440
oversized homes, constant upgrades, then

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:49.840
you don't ever get to play offense.

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:52.080
Staying low profile creates liquidity

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:54.479
and that ultimately creates peace of

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:56.560
mind and it creates options. Reason

00:05:54.479 --> 00:05:58.080
number four, compounding does all the

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:59.280
heavy lifting. And this one is the one

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:01.280
that most people completely

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:03.360
underestimate. But small, boring

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:05.840
decisions repeated consistently turn

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:08.639
into massive outcomes. Here's a simple

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:11.360
example. If you start with just $100 and

00:06:08.639 --> 00:06:14.160
you contribute $100 a month and invest

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:17.199
it for 30 years at the S&P 500's

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:18.960
historical average of about 10% over a

00:06:17.199 --> 00:06:20.880
long enough period of time, you don't

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:25.639
end up with a couple of grand, 10 grand,

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:25.639
20 grand. You end up with $199,137.

00:06:26.479 --> 00:06:30.240
And think about that. It's a $100 a

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:32.080
month that we're talking about. Like

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:34.479
what if you did 500? What if you did

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:36.960
a,000? Can you imagine? It came from

00:06:34.479 --> 00:06:39.360
consistency and not sabotaging yourself

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:42.080
with lifestyle upgrades along the way.

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:44.160
That extra $100 a month is usually what

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:46.000
people spend trying to go out and be

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:48.720
with the who's who. And when you don't

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:50.720
spend it, it compounds into options

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:52.240
later on in life. So, look, I'm not

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:53.840
saying that you should never enjoy your

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:55.600
money. I'm not saying that you need to

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:58.080
live like a monk and we have to go back

00:06:55.600 --> 00:07:00.560
to like this minimalism, you know, thing

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:02.400
forever. Once you're actually wealthy

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:03.919
and you have a lot of money in savings,

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:06.560
investments, and you have a lot of

00:07:03.919 --> 00:07:07.840
liquid cash and real security, then you

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:09.599
can buy all the nice things that you

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:11.199
want. I'm just saying buy them with

00:07:09.599 --> 00:07:13.120
cash. You know, don't overleverage

00:07:11.199 --> 00:07:15.120
yourself. Don't go into massive amounts

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:17.599
of debt trying to look cool or keep up

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:19.759
with the Joneses, but instead buy them

00:07:17.599 --> 00:07:21.599
from a position of strength. There's a

00:07:19.759 --> 00:07:23.440
huge difference between driving a luxury

00:07:21.599 --> 00:07:25.280
car because you actually like the car

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:27.440
that you're driving and driving one

00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:29.759
because you need to feel validated by

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:32.080
society. Looking successful and building

00:07:29.759 --> 00:07:34.240
real wealth are rarely the same thing.

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:36.800
And if you want freedom later, then you

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:38.319
need to resist a lot of the upgrades

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:40.319
right now. That's why they call it

00:07:38.319 --> 00:07:41.680
delayed gratification. If you like the

00:07:40.319 --> 00:07:43.599
video, I really appreciate it. Go ahead

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:45.520
and watch this video right here. I think

00:07:43.599 --> 00:07:46.720
it would really help you. Subscribe if

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:48.960
you haven't already, and I'll see you in

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:48.960
the next

